<p xid="959"><c props="font-style:italic">We have addUser.controller.js</c><c props="font-style:italic"></c></p>
<p xid="961"><c props="font-style:italic"></c><c></c></p>
<p xid="962"><c props="font-weight:bold">Here we have already been handling the req body. As below:</c><c props="font-weight:bold"></c></p>
<p xid="963"><c></c><c></c></p>
<p xid="964"><c props="bgcolor:c0c0c0">const {name, email, password} = req.body();</c><c props="bgcolor:c0c0c0"></c></p>
<p xid="965"><c></c><c></c></p>
<p xid="966">Since we have used multer middlerware and placed that in router, router will also attach the files with request if any files uploaded by user. </p>
<p xid="967"><c></c><c></c></p>
<p xid="968"><c props="font-weight:bold">We will handle the files in in controller.</c><c props="font-weight:bold"></c></p>
<p xid="969"><c></c><c></c></p>
<p xid="970"><c props="bgcolor:c0c0c0">const filesData = req.files;</c><c props="bgcolor:c0c0c0"></c></p>
<p xid="971"><c></c><c></c></p>
<p xid="972">handles files in more specific way:</p>
<p xid="973"><c></c><c></c></p>
<p xid="974"><c props="bgcolor:c0c0c0">const bannerImg = filesData.bannerImg?.[0]?.filename || null ;</c><c props="bgcolor:c0c0c0"></c></p>
<p xid="975"><c props="bgcolor:c0c0c0">const roomImgs = filesData.roomImgs?.map(file=&gt;file.filename) || [ ] ;</c><c props="bgcolor:c0c0c0"></c></p>
<p xid="960"><c></c><c></c></p>
<p xid="976"><c></c><c></c></p>
<p xid="977"><c></c><c></c></p>
<p xid="401">--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------<c></c></p>
<p xid="402">Logic Building<c></c></p>
<p xid="403">The steps in logic involed:<c></c></p>
<p xid="404">1. Get the user details from frontend<c></c></p>
<p xid="405">2. Validation - Check if not empty etc etc<c></c></p>
<p xid="406">3. Check if that room category already exist<c></c></p>
<p xid="407">4. check for images if uplaoded on server or not<c></c></p>
<p xid="408">5. upload images to cloudinary and check if uploaded succesfully on cloudinary or not<c></c></p>
<p xid="409">6. Create a room category object - create entry in db<c></c></p>
<p xid="410">7. Remove password and refresh token feild from response.<c></c></p>
<p xid="411">8. Check for room category creation<c></c></p>
<p xid="412">9. return res<c></c></p>
<p xid="413">Create a controller which will read the req.body and process thet information.<c></c></p>
<p xid="414">examples:<c></c></p>
<p xid="415">const addUser = asyncHandler((req,res, next)=&amp;gt;{<c></c></p>
<p xid="416">const {name. email, password } = req.body;<c></c></p>
<p xid="417">export default addUser;<c></c></p>
<p xid="418">In above example this controller will be passed to router , where router will invoke the<c></c></p>
<p xid="419">post<c></c></p>
<p xid="420">request.<c></c></p>
<p xid="421">Router logic:<c></c></p>
<p xid="422">import addUser from ‘../controllers/addUser.controller.js";<c></c></p>
<p xid="423">import express from “express”;<c></c></p>
<p xid="424">const router = express.Router();<c></c></p>
<p xid="425">router.post(“/user”, addUser)<c></c></p>
<p xid="426">export default router;<c></c></p>
<p xid="427">S<c></c></p>
<p xid="428">er<c></c></p>
<p xid="429">ve<c></c></p>
<p xid="430">r.js<c></c></p>
<p xid="431">import userRouter from “./Router/userRouter.js”;<c></c></p>
<p xid="432">//Need middleware to process the json data<c></c></p>
<p xid="433">app.use(express.json());<c></c></p>
<p xid="434">app.use(“/api”,<c></c></p>
<p xid="435">userRouter<c></c></p>
<p xid="436">);<c></c></p>
<p xid="437">Validation will be done in controller. Like as below<c></c></p>
<p xid="438">import {ApiError} from ‘./util/ApiError.js’;<c></c></p>
<p xid="439">const addUser = asyncHandler((req, res, next)=&amp;gt;{<c></c></p>
<p xid="440">const {name, email, password} = req.body;<c></c></p>
<p xid="441">if([name,email, password].some((field)=&amp;gt; field.trim()==="”))<c></c></p>
<p xid="442">throw new ApiError(400,"All fields are required”);<c></c></p>
<p xid="443">In this situiation we will be directly checking with database if any same room category already exit.<c></c></p>
<p xid="444">Here we will communicate with the db with the help of mongoose model.<c></c></p>
<p xid="445">So while admin add the new room category, I will check if that room name or room code already exist<c></c></p>
<p xid="446">I will do like this<c></c></p>
<p xid="447">We have a model created and exported<c></c></p>
<p xid="448">export const RoomCategory = mongoose.model("RoomCategory", roomCategorySchema);<c></c></p>
<p xid="449">We will consider only 4 input data as of now for sample<c></c></p>
<p xid="450">I can create a controller like<c></c></p>
<p xid="451">import { RoomCategory } from ‘../models/roomCategory.model.js”;<c></c></p>
<p xid="452">const roomController = ayncHandler((req, res, next)=&amp;gt;{<c></c></p>
<p xid="453">const {name, code, location, info} = req.body;<c></c></p>
<p xid="454">//validation done to check if its not empty<c></c></p>
<p xid="455">// check if duplicate name or code.<c></c></p>
<p xid="456">const existingCategory = RoomCategory.findOne({<c></c></p>
<p xid="457">$or: [{name}, {code}]<c></c></p>
<p xid="458">if(existingCategory){<c></c></p>
<p xid="459">throw new ApiError(409, “Category or category code already exist”)};<c></c></p>
<p xid="460">I<c></c></p>
<p xid="461">n<c></c></p>
<p xid="462">above example we have directly checked the existing data or duplication with database.<c></c></p>
<p xid="463">4. Use multer middleware to upload the images or files etc.<c></c></p>
<p xid="464">This operation wil be done in the router. Bcoz router has specified the route and the request time.<c></c></p>
